    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d229">

                <pb facs="0316" n="236" xml:id="pg236"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. White to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1901-12-20"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">December 20, 1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 726.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to my dispatch No. 721, of
                    10th instant, I inclose copies of a letter which I have received from Mr.
                    Barratt, counsel for Mr. Charles Lilrywhite, of the one inclosed therewith from
                    the latter, and of the cablegram<anchor n="a" xml:id="d229-f1"/> which I
                    thereupon sent you, asking whether I might, in accordance with his wishes,
                    inform His Majesty’s Government that we accept the amount offered in settlement
                    of his claim and hand it over to him.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry White.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d229-a1.xml" xpointer="d229-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d229-a2.xml" xpointer="d229-a2"/>
